It re-implements marked's lexer, inline parser and renderer for speed —
index-gated block dispatch, first-character inline dispatch, and a
single-pass renderer — while following marked's grammar and rendering
decisions exactly, so that parse(markdown) returns the same HTML as
marked.parse(markdown) with marked's default options. marked's grammar
patterns are retained where a regular expression is the clearest
statement of a rule. marked is distributed under the MIT License; the
